# Testing Guidelines

Reusable testing guidelines for Java, Spring Boot, and AI/RAG features. Apply them when writing or changing tests.

## Test pyramid

- Prefer unit tests for domain and business logic.
- Use Spring slice tests for one layer at a time: `@WebMvcTest` for the web layer, `@DataJpaTest` for persistence.
- Use `@SpringBootTest` with Testcontainers when a test must exercise the application with real infrastructure.

## Deterministic behaviour

- Assert exact values for deterministic logic.
- Cover every valid state transition and every invalid state transition with its own test.

## Probabilistic AI output

- Evaluate probabilistic AI output with an evaluation set and acceptance thresholds.
- Do not assert exact string matches on generated text.
- Run AI evaluation tests against a real model in a separate, explicitly tagged suite that is excluded from the default build.

## External models

- Tests never call paid or external LLM or embedding APIs.
- Stub those clients.

## Test design

- Name tests after the behaviour they describe.
- Structure each test as Arrange-Act-Assert.
- Keep tests independent. Do not share mutable data between tests.

## Failing tests

- Never weaken, skip, or delete a failing test to make it pass.
